{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"737a334f4b239e52","name":"card_event_evasive_action","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Breakthrough/events/card_event_evasive_action","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EVASIVE ACTION","text":"Trigger this card when the enemy deploys a unit with a deployment effect. Cancel the effect.","flavorText":"The “Corkscrew” was a defensive maneuver developed to help bombers to defend against attacking fighters, mostly against night fighters. The manoeuvre involved a high speed spiral, turning and diving, sometimes 600-1000 ft, followed by a steep climb and then to roll and repeat the manoeuvre. The dive was intended to pull enough G-force that it would tear off the wings of a fighter. Another evasive maneuver was the “Barrel Roll” which involved slowing down the forward motion by doing a Helical Roll around a straight flightpath. This would often force an attacking fighter to overshoot the bomber and fly out in front.","faction":"Britain","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Common","cost":0,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"Name":"card_event_evasive_action","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_evasive_action_title","SourceString":"EVASIVE ACTION","LocalizedString":"EVASIVE ACTION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_evasive_action_text","SourceString":"Trigger this card when the enemy deploys a unit with a deployment effect. Cancel the effect.","LocalizedString":"Trigger this card when the enemy deploys a unit with a deployment effect. Cancel the effect."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_evasive_action_history","SourceString":"The “Corkscrew” was a defensive maneuver developed to help bombers to defend against attacking fighters, mostly against night fighters. The manoeuvre involved a high speed spiral, turning and diving, sometimes 600-1000 ft, followed by a steep climb and then to roll and repeat the manoeuvre. The dive was intended to pull enough G-force that it would tear off the wings of a fighter. Another evasive maneuver was the “Barrel Roll” which involved slowing down the forward motion by doing a Helical Roll around a straight flightpath. This would often force an attacking fighter to overshoot the bomber and fly out in front.","LocalizedString":"The “Corkscrew” was a defensive maneuver developed to help bombers to defend against attacking fighters, mostly against night fighters. The manoeuvre involved a high speed spiral, turning and diving, sometimes 600-1000 ft, followed by a steep climb and then to roll and repeat the manoeuvre. The dive was intended to pull enough G-force that it would tear off the wings of a fighter. Another evasive maneuver was the “Barrel Roll” which involved slowing down the forward motion by doing a Helical Roll around a straight flightpath. This would often force an attacking fighter to overshoot the bomber and fly out in front."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isInPermanentPool":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardDeploymentTrigger"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Breakthrough/t_britsh_flyboat.t_britsh_flyboat","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Rebellion","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/EVASIVE_ACTION.EVASIVE_ACTION","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":411.0,"Y":512.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_evasive_action_photo","SourceString